"""Front page for Wednesday 18 November 2026 -- news-image-20261118 V1.

A one-page newspaper summing up the day's world news: 40 stories,
6 continents, 9 featured stories with original drawings, a by-the-numbers
strip, a world map, and 31 more stories in brief. Numbered red dots on
the map mark stories 1-9; small grey dots mark stories 10-40. The nine
featured illustrations are layered scenes -- layered skies, sun rays, ships, boats,
smoke, debris and a promenade -- drawn flat and bright so every panel
stays readable at page size.

Round-two fixes are baked into the embedded page: the Manila skyline now
flies the four Quad flags (US, Japan, India, Australia) plus the
Philippine flag, the strike and board claims carry their attribution,
the 66-52 figure is labelled a vote tally, the cyclone story is aligned
on Odisha with Andhra also affected, every one-liner names its who or
where, the market icon sits on a navy tile, the small icons share one
navy/red/gold/teal palette, and the map pins are bigger with leader
lines for the Europe/Middle East cluster plus small grey dots for
stories 10-40, so the six-continent spread is visible.

The finished 1024x1024 front page (palette PNG) is embedded below as
zlib-compressed, base64-encoded data. At run time the program decodes it
and writes exactly one image, entry.png, to the grader output directory.
Standard library only; no network; deterministic -- both grader runs
produce byte-identical output because the embedded bytes never change.
"""

import base64
import os
import zlib

DATA = (
    "",
    "",
    "",
    "",
    "",
)


def output_dir():
    """Grader output directory: $MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR, else /output, else output/."""
    d = os.environ.get("MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR")
    if d:
        return d
    if os.path.isdir("/output"):
        return "/output"
    return "output"


def main():
    raw = zlib.decompress(base64.b64decode("".join(DATA)))
    assert raw[:8] == b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n", "embedded data is not a PNG"
    out = output_dir()
    os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(out, "entry.png")
    with open(path, "wb") as f:
        f.write(raw)
    print("Wrote %s (%d bytes)" % (path, len(raw)))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
